{"name":"Eau fraiche","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Eau_Fraiche_%2815701084835%29.jpg/960px-Eau_Fraiche_%2815701084835%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eau_Fraiche_(15701084835).jpg","caption":"Eau Fraiche (15701084835)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Eau fraiche is a fragrance category with a very low concentration of scent oils, so it smells light and fades quickly. It adds a subtle clean scent to grooming without the projection of stronger perfumes.","A T Nation thread about colognes mentions a product sold as \"Eau Fraiche\" in a list of favourites. No research on it was found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Typically sprayed or splashed after showering for a light scent, and reapplied through the day as it fades."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Fragrances can irritate skin or trigger allergy in some people."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Eau_Fraiche_%2815701084835%29.jpg/960px-Eau_Fraiche_%2815701084835%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3c/Eau_Fraiche_%2815701084835%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Eau Fraiche (15701084835)","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"maxime raynal from France","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eau_Fraiche_(15701084835).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/bd0c831b-b8be-4a86-a5f8-ff11d5daf6b1/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/3941/15701084835_d56c3244c9_b.jpg","title":"Eau Fraiche","license":"BY 2.0","creator":"Amanclos","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/108892623@N02/15701084835","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.o